<deployment.md>
    a schema:TechArticle ;
    schema:isPartOf <#the-code> ;
    schema:position 50 ;
    dcterms:abstract "the static build, deployed to GitHub Pages by CI for each released version, or published by hand to any web space."@en .

<configuration.md>
    a schema:TechArticle ;
    schema:isPartOf <#the-code> ;
    schema:position 60 ;
    dcterms:abstract "the VITE_ settings a build reads (the app's name, the repository the footer and the page link to, the Pod providers, the deck library), their defaults, how to set them, and what they do not reach."@en .

<reuse.md>
    a schema:TechArticle ;
    schema:isPartOf <#the-code> ;
    schema:position 70 ;
    dcterms:abstract "running your own instance: fork, configure, build, host anywhere, make the deck library your own, the files to edit by hand, and the names that must stay because they are part of the data."@en .

<style.md>
    a schema:TechArticle ;
    schema:isPartOf <#the-code> ;
    schema:position 80 ;
    dcterms:abstract "how the code, Turtle, docs and commit messages are written: formatting and linting with Biome, TypeScript, naming, the Turtle house style, comments, plain English with American spelling, and English as the authoritative language."@en .

<releasing.md>
    a schema:TechArticle ;
    schema:isPartOf <#the-code> ;
    schema:position 90 ;
    dcterms:abstract "how the app's versions are chosen (SemVer, from 1.0.0, by semantic-release from the commits' Conventional Commits types), what counts as breaking for data in pods, what a release does and the deploy key it pushes with, what to do when one fails, and how the app's version differs from those of the vocabulary, shapes and decks."@en .

